    "readme": "# neuro/ieeg/ieeg\n\nDRAFT — generated from BIDS v1.11.2 by aimport/tools/draft_datatypes.py; check the brainlife registry for an existing datatype before registering.\n\nUses BIDS as the datatype: files are named as in BIDS, BIDS datatype `ieeg`, suffix `ieeg`.\n\nSource: BIDS specification v1.11.2, raw data, `ieeg/*_ieeg`.\n\nExactly one of: .mefd; .edf; .vhdr + .eeg + .vmrk; .set + .fdt; .nwb must be present (alternative data formats, none is marked required).\n\nThe JSON sidecar is required (the schema requires metadata fields in it).\n\nRelated BIDS files in `ieeg/` (separate datatypes, not part of this one): `channels`, `coordsystem`, `electrodes`, `events`, `photo`, `physio`, `physioevents`, `stim`.\n\n"
